# The owner reviews what bounds swarm-workspace-deployer (docs/workspaces.md
# §2.4, safeguard 2; #847).
#
# That identity holds project-wide account-IAM power in a project shared with
# another team, and Google cannot narrow it. Since WD2's re-decision
# (2026-10-10) the Cloud Run job swarm-workspace-apply runs as it, from the
# workspace-apply image, and that image carries what the identity will do: the
# entrypoint that scrubs every override (entry.py), the job's script
# (workspace-apply.sh), the call guard, its rules and shims, the script it
# runs, the library both source, and the Dockerfile and build config that
# decide what the image holds. A merge reaches the identity only when the owner's bootstrap
# apply moves the image digest; this review is the step before that. Branch
# protection must require the code owner's review for these paths, or this
# file is only a suggestion (the owner's setting, not this repository's).

